    "created_at": "2016-03-30T09:05:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-30T09:05:54Z",
    "body": "There are two ways to handle this:\n- Like an old-school fast-forward/rewind tape-based player: if you fast forward (i.e. playback rate > 1), you can go back to play at speed 1 using \"play\" and there something that shows you you're fast forwarding.\n- Like it is now everywhere but in Gecko, play/pause resets the `playbackRate`.\n\nNote that UA's interfaces are supposed to use the [`defaultPlaybackRate`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-media-defaultplaybackrate) anyways, so it should not be reset (or more accurately, the `playbackRate` must be reset to the `defaultPlaybackRate`, which in effect is what we want). \n\nI think Gecko's behaviour is a bug that has to be fixed on our side.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
